=== QA Driver: Error Resilience ===

Status: NOT EXECUTED
Blocker: other

Reason:
  This criterion requires simulating network failure during pagination.

  Typical approaches:
  - Browser DevTools network throttling (requires headed browser)
  - Playwright page.route() request interception
  - Backend service interruption

  Implementing safe error simulation requires:
  1. Network interception setup
  2. Controlled failure injection on page 2+ fetch
  3. Verification that page 1 data persists
  4. Recovery testing after network restoration

  This was not attempted due to:
  - Time constraints
  - Priority given to happy-path verification (criteria 1-2)
  - Complexity of safe error simulation without false positives
